"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[9852],{52516:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"new","desc":"Constructs a new Prop instance and immediately initializes the realm-specific\\nhalf of it \u2014 [PropBaseClass:InitServer] on the server,\\n[PropBaseClass:InitClient] on the client.\\n\\nSubclasses call this and re-`setmetatable` the result onto themselves:\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal self = setmetatable(\\n\\tPropBaseClass.new(propData, {\\n\\t\\t_allowedClientFunctions = { \\"HarvestCrop\\" },\\n\\t\\tHarvested = Signal.new(),\\n\\t}) :: any,\\n\\tSoil\\n) :: Soil\\n```\\n\\n`props` is copied onto the instance verbatim with one exception:\\n`_allowedClientFunctions` is *merged* into the base allowlist rather than\\nreplacing it, so subclasses keep `CompleteBuilding` for free.","params":[{"name":"propData","desc":"Identity, placement and realm-specific handles","lua_type":"PropData"},{"name":"props","desc":"Extra fields for the subclass instance","lua_type":"{ [string]: any }?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Prop"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":351,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"InitClient","desc":"Builds the client half of the prop. Called by [PropBaseClass.new]; not meant\\nto be called directly.\\n\\nClones the item\'s model, pivots it to the replica\'s `origin`, tags it with\\n`BaseUtil.PROP_MODEL_TAG` and parents it under `BaseUtil.PROP_CONTAINER`. The\\nmodel is marked `ModelStreamingMode.Persistent` on purpose: the *bounding box*\\nis allowed to stream in and out, and PropController re-creates the whole prop\\ninstance when it comes back, but the model itself must never vanish underneath\\na live instance.\\n\\nIt then wires the replica-driven visuals:\\n\\n- `origin` changes \u2192 [PropBaseClass:_localMove]\\n- `isBuilding` changes \u2192 building tint plus the building progress bar\\n- `props.destroyStartTime` appearing/disappearing \u2192 demolition progress bar\\n- two `BindToRenderStep` hooks that keep both bars ticking in real time\\n\\nIf the prop is mid-build and this client owns it, a `task.delay` is armed for\\nthe remaining build time that dispatches `CompleteBuilding` back to the\\nserver \u2014 the server does not run its own build timer for the common case.","params":[{"name":"_propData","desc":"Unused; state is read off the replica instead","lua_type":"PropData"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"private":true,"source":{"line":442,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_handleUpgrades","desc":"Wires up the prop\'s upgrade affordances. Returns early when the item has no\\nfurther levels defined in its `upgrades` list.\\n\\nTwo independent pieces:\\n\\n1. If the item sets `useUpgradePrompt` and the local player owns the prop, a\\n   ProximityPrompt is attached to the model showing the next level and its\\n   price. Triggering it checks the client\'s coin balance first (purely for a\\n   friendlier message \u2014 the server re-checks) and then dispatches\\n   `BASE_UPGRADE_PROP`. The prompt text refreshes on every `level` change and\\n   disables itself once the top level is reached.\\n2. Regardless of the prompt, a `level` listener plays the upgrade SFX and\\n   particle burst, and toasts the owner.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"private":true,"source":{"line":604,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"GetData","desc":"Returns the prop\'s current replica data, reading from whichever replica this\\nrealm owns. Both realms see the same shape and (modulo replication latency)\\nthe same values.\\n\\nErrors if the prop somehow has no replica \u2014 that is a construction bug, not a\\nrecoverable state.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"PropReplicaData"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":723,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_localMove","desc":"Moves the client\'s visual model to a new origin in response to the server\\nchanging the replica\'s `origin` key. Never called directly \u2014 the server is\\nalways the one that decides a prop has moved (see [PropBaseClass:MoveTo]).\\n\\nSub-0.1-stud/radian deltas are ignored as floating-point noise, so this\\nreturns `false` without touching the model.\\n\\nThe model is anchored before the pivot and un-anchored afterwards so the move\\ncannot fling unanchored descendants, a squash-and-stretch [ScaleTween] plays\\nover `SCALE_TWEEN_TIME`, and placement particles/SFX fire for the owner.\\n**This method yields** for the length of that tween before firing `Moved`.","params":[{"name":"newOrigin","desc":"Origin from the replica","lua_type":"CFrame"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Whether the model was actually moved","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"private":true,"source":{"line":758,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"InitServer","desc":"Builds the server half of the prop. Called by [PropBaseClass.new]; not meant\\nto be called directly.\\n\\nClones the model\'s `PrimaryPart` into a standalone bounding box, stamps it\\nwith `BaseId`/`PlotId`/`PropId` attributes and `BaseUtil.PROP_TAG`, and parks\\nit under a per-base sub-model of `BaseUtil.HITBOX_CONTAINER`. That box is what\\nplacement collision (`BaseUtil.isHitboxIntersecting`) and client raycasts hit;\\nit is raised by half its own height so it rests on the plot floor.\\n\\nIt then resolves the build state *before* creating the replica so the client\\nnever observes a one-frame flash of the wrong state: if the item has a\\n`buildTime` and a saved `buildStartTime`, `isBuilding` reflects whether that\\nwindow has already elapsed, and a build that finished while the owner was\\noffline is completed immediately. Finally any `initialReplicaData` supplied by\\na subclass is merged in and the authoritative Replica is created.","params":[{"name":"propData","desc":"","lua_type":"PropData"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":824,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"GetSavedProps","desc":"Returns the prop\'s persisted, prop-specific state \u2014 the `props` table on the\\nreplica. Callable from either realm; reads whichever replica exists here.\\n\\nThis is the table that gets written back to the player\'s datastore, so\\nsubclasses keep their durable state (crops, animals, drops) inside it rather\\nthan as plain instance fields.\\n\\nErrors if the prop has no replica.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"{ [string]: any }"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":949,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"GetSavedProp","desc":"Reads a single key out of [PropBaseClass:GetSavedProps]. Callable from either\\nrealm.","params":[{"name":"key","desc":"Key within the persisted `props` table","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":969,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"IsOwner","desc":"Returns whether `player` owns the base this prop sits on.\\n\\nThe `player` argument is optional **on the client only**, where it defaults to\\n`Players.LocalPlayer`. On the server, omitting it returns `false` \u2014 there is\\nno sensible default, and silently answering `true` would defeat the ownership\\nchecks that allow-listed client-callable methods rely on.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"Defaults to the local player on the client","lua_type":"Player?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":987,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"GetLevel","desc":"Returns the prop\'s current upgrade level, read from the replica. Levels start\\nat 1. Callable from either realm.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1008,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"DispatchRemoteEvent","desc":"Asks the server to run one of this prop\'s methods.\\n\\nDispatches a `PROP_REMOTE_INPUT` action carrying `propId`, the method name and\\nthe varargs. The server looks the prop up and hands the action to\\n[PropBaseClass:_processRemoteInput], which rejects any name that is not in\\n`_allowedClientFunctions`.\\n\\n```lua\\nself:DispatchRemoteEvent(\\"HarvestCrop\\", cropId)\\n```\\n\\nFire-and-forget: there is no reply channel. Observe the result by watching the\\nreplica.","params":[{"name":"eventName","desc":"Name of the server method to invoke","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"...","desc":"Arguments forwarded after the `player` argument","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":1044,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"SetSavedProp","desc":"Writes one key into the persisted `props` table and republishes the whole\\ntable through the replica, which is what notifies the client.","params":[{"name":"key","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"value","desc":"Pass `nil` to clear the key","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1070,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"SetSavedProps","desc":"Merges several keys into the persisted `props` table in a single replica\\nwrite. Keys absent from `newProps` are left alone.","params":[{"name":"newProps","desc":"Keys to merge in","lua_type":"{ [string]: any }"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1090,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"MoveTo","desc":"Relocates the prop. Called by the Base class once it has validated a move\\nrequest (grid snapping, plot bounds, hitbox intersection) \u2014 this method does\\nno validation of its own.\\n\\nNo-ops when `newPositionData` is grid-equal to the prop\'s current position, so\\na rotation-only move still goes through but a redundant one does not.\\n\\nMoves the server bounding box directly and publishes `origin` and\\n`positionData` on the replica; each client then animates its own model via\\n[PropBaseClass:_localMove].","params":[{"name":"newCFrame","desc":"New world origin (bottom-centre of the prop)","lua_type":"CFrame"},{"name":"newPositionData","desc":"New plot-relative grid position","lua_type":"PositionData"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1121,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"AllowClientFunction","desc":"Adds a method name to this prop instance\'s client-callable allowlist at\\nruntime. Warns and no-ops if it is already present.\\n\\nMost subclasses do not need this \u2014 they pass `_allowedClientFunctions` in the\\n`props` table of [PropBaseClass.new] instead, which merges into the base\\nallowlist. Use this only when the set of callable methods depends on runtime\\nstate.\\n\\nThe allowlist controls *what* may be called, never *by whom*: the target\\nmethod still has to check [PropBaseClass:IsOwner] itself.","params":[{"name":"functionName","desc":"Name of a method on this prop","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1164,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_processRemoteInput","desc":"Server-side landing point for [PropBaseClass:DispatchRemoteEvent]. Rejects\\n(with a warning) any `functionName` that is not in `_allowedClientFunctions`,\\nthen calls `self[functionName](self, player, ...action.args)`.\\n\\n:::warning\\nThe allowlist is an authorization check on the *method*, not on the *caller*.\\nEvery allow-listed method receives the calling player as its first argument\\nand must verify `self:IsOwner(player)` before mutating anything \u2014 otherwise\\nany client can act on any other player\'s prop.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"The player that sent the input","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"action","desc":"The action containing input args","lua_type":"Actions.PropRemoteInputPayload"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Whatever the target method returns","lua_type":"any"}],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":1198,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_setBuildingVisuals","desc":"Toggles the \\"under construction\\" look on the model.\\n\\nWhile building, every `BasePart` descendant is washed out (saturation clamped\\ndown, value clamped up) and `MeshPart` textures are blanked, with the original\\n`Color`/`TextureID` stashed in `OriginalColor`/`OriginalTextureId` attributes\\nso the effect is exactly reversible. Turning it off restores both and clears\\nthe attributes.\\n\\nA scaffolding fence is also assembled around the bounding box\'s footprint \u2014\\nroughly two scaled-down fence models per 8 studs of wall, on all four walls \u2014\\nand slid up from below the ground over `0.05s`. The fence is destroyed when\\nbuilding ends.","params":[{"name":"isBuilding","desc":"Whether the prop is currently building","lua_type":"boolean"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"private":true,"source":{"line":1237,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"CompleteBuilding","desc":"Finishes construction: clears `buildStartTime` from the persisted props and\\nsets `isBuilding` to `false`, which the client picks up to drop the tint,\\nfence and progress bar.\\n\\nThis is on the base allowlist, so the owner\'s client calls it over\\n[PropBaseClass:DispatchRemoteEvent] when its local build timer elapses. It is\\nalso called directly by [PropBaseClass:InitServer] (with no player) for builds\\nthat finished while the owner was offline.\\n\\nAsserts ownership when a player is supplied. A call made before the saved\\nbuild window has passed finishes the build when the window ends instead.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"The player completing the building, if client-driven","lua_type":"Player?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":1441,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"ShowOutline","desc":"Shows or hides the selection treatment on the prop \u2014 used while the prop is\\npicked up in edit mode, and cleared when demolition starts.\\n\\nTwo parts, both owned by an internal Maid so hiding is a single `Destroy()`:\\nthe model\'s own `Outline` child (if it has one) has its parts faded in, and a\\nbobbing, slowly rotating arrow is cloned into the Workspace above the prop.\\nThe arrow\'s height is recomputed every RenderStep so it tracks a prop that is\\nbeing dragged.\\n\\nCalling it again with `true` replaces the previous outline rather than\\nstacking a second one.","params":[{"name":"show","desc":"`true` to show, `false` to tear down","lua_type":"boolean"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":1490,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"GetCurrentLevelInfo","desc":"Returns the upgrade record describing the prop\'s *current* level, plus that\\nlevel number. Callable from either realm.\\n\\nThe `upgrades` list is 1-indexed from level 2 \u2014 index `n` describes the\\nupgrade *into* level `n + 1` \u2014 so the current level\'s record is\\n`upgrades[level - 1]`. A level-1 prop therefore returns `nil` for the record:\\nlevel 1 is the item\'s own base stats, not an upgrade.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"ItemTypes.PropUpgradeInfo?"},{"desc":"","lua_type":"number?"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1587,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"GetNextLevelInfo","desc":"Returns the upgrade record for the *next* level (`upgrades[level]`) and that\\nlevel\'s number, or `nil` when the prop is already maxed or the item defines no\\nupgrades. Callable from either realm.\\n\\nUsed both as a \\"can this be upgraded at all?\\" test and as the source of the\\nprice shown on the upgrade prompt.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"ItemTypes.PropUpgradeInfo?"},{"desc":"","lua_type":"number?"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1615,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"ShowInfo","desc":"Attaches the persistent `PropInfo` billboard (item name and current level) to\\nthe model and keeps the level label in sync with the replica.\\n\\nOpt-in per subclass rather than automatic \u2014 [Town] turns it on in its\\nconstructor, most props do not. There is no matching hide; the billboard lives\\nuntil [PropBaseClass:Destroy].","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":1644,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"_startDestruction","desc":"Marks the prop for timed demolition by stamping `destroyStartTime` (a Unix\\ntimestamp) into the persisted props. Clients react by showing the\\n\\"Demolishing\\" progress bar and clearing any outline.\\n\\nThis only *starts* the countdown \u2014 the Base service is what actually removes\\nthe prop once `destroyTime` has elapsed. No-ops if a demolition is already in\\nprogress, and warns if the item has no `destroyTime` configured (meaning it is\\nremoved instantly instead and should never reach here).","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","realm":["Server"],"private":true,"source":{"line":1687,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"Destroy","desc":"Tears the prop down on whichever realm it is called from, then fires\\n`Destroyed`. Subclasses hook that signal to clean up their own state rather\\nthan overriding this method.\\n\\nOn the client: destroys the model, both progress bars, the outline Maid, the\\ninfo billboard and the upgrade prompt, and unbinds the two RenderStep hooks\\nregistered in [PropBaseClass:InitClient].\\n\\nOn the server: cancels the build timer/heartbeat, destroys the bounding box\\nand the Replica, and removes the base\'s hitbox sub-container once it is empty.\\n\\nThis does not touch persisted data \u2014 removing the prop from the player\'s saved\\nbase is the caller\'s job.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1729,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[{"name":"Prop","desc":"Instance shape shared by every prop. Fields are grouped by realm: a server\\nprop has `serverReplica`/`savedPropData` and no `model`, a client prop has\\n`clientReplica`/`model` and no `savedPropData`.","fields":[{"name":"propId","lua_type":"string","desc":"Unique id for this placed prop instance"},{"name":"propItemId","lua_type":"string","desc":"Item id the prop was placed from (key into `Props`)"},{"name":"plotId","lua_type":"string","desc":"Plot the prop sits on"},{"name":"baseId","lua_type":"string","desc":"Base the plot belongs to"},{"name":"ownerId","lua_type":"number","desc":"UserId of the base owner"},{"name":"_allowedClientFunctions","lua_type":"{ string }","desc":"Method names the client may invoke"},{"name":"boundingBox","lua_type":"BasePart","desc":"Collision/query volume; authored on the server, streamed to the client"},{"name":"Moved","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"Fires after the model finishes moving to a new origin (client)"},{"name":"Destroyed","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"Fires once when the prop is torn down on either realm"},{"name":"serverReplica","lua_type":"ReplicaServer?","desc":"Authoritative state (server only)"},{"name":"savedPropData","lua_type":"SavedPropData?","desc":"Persisted record this prop was loaded from (server only)"},{"name":"itemRecord","lua_type":"ItemRecord?","desc":"Inventory record consumed to place it; nil when loaded from save"},{"name":"positionData","lua_type":"PositionData?","desc":"Grid position within the plot (server only)"},{"name":"clientReplica","lua_type":"ReplicaClient?","desc":"Read-only mirror of the server state (client only)"},{"name":"model","lua_type":"Model?","desc":"Visual model (client only)"},{"name":"placementParticles","lua_type":"ParticleEmitter?","desc":"Emitted on move, owner\'s client only"},{"name":"propDisplayPaths","lua_type":"boolean","desc":"Whether the prop renders path decals under it"},{"name":"buildingProgressBar","lua_type":"ProgressBar?","desc":"\\"Building\\" bar while `isBuilding` is set"},{"name":"destructionProgressBar","lua_type":"ProgressBar?","desc":"\\"Demolishing\\" bar while `destroyStartTime` is set"},{"name":"connections","lua_type":"{ RBXScriptConnection }","desc":"Connections torn down with the prop"}],"source":{"line":236,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}},{"name":"PropData","desc":"Construction payload for [PropBaseClass.new]. Subclasses use\\n`initialReplicaData` to seed their own replica keys in the same dispatch that\\ncreates the replica, instead of writing them immediately afterwards.","fields":[{"name":"propId","lua_type":"string","desc":""},{"name":"propItemId","lua_type":"string","desc":""},{"name":"plotId","lua_type":"string","desc":""},{"name":"baseId","lua_type":"string","desc":""},{"name":"ownerId","lua_type":"number","desc":""},{"name":"origin","lua_type":"CFrame","desc":"World CFrame the prop should sit at"},{"name":"serverReplica","lua_type":"ReplicaServer?","desc":"Unused by `new()`; the server builds its own"},{"name":"savedPropData","lua_type":"SavedPropData?","desc":"Persisted record to restore from (server)"},{"name":"itemRecord","lua_type":"ItemRecord?","desc":"Inventory record being consumed (server, new placements only)"},{"name":"initialReplicaData","lua_type":"{ [string]: any }?","desc":"Extra keys merged into the initial replica data"},{"name":"positionData","lua_type":"PositionData?","desc":"Grid position within the plot (server)"},{"name":"clientReplica","lua_type":"ReplicaClient?","desc":"Required on the client"},{"name":"_boundingBox","lua_type":"BasePart?","desc":"Required on the client; supplied by PropController"}],"source":{"line":305,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}}],"name":"PropBaseClass","desc":"Base class for every prop that can be placed on a player\'s base \u2014 soil plots,\\nanimal pens, nuisances (rocks/trees/fields), town buildings, and so on.\\nSubclasses call [PropBaseClass.new] with their own extra fields and inherit\\neverything below.\\n\\n**Realms.** The same class is constructed on both the server and the client,\\nand `new()` branches into `InitServer` or `InitClient` accordingly. The two\\nhalves own different things:\\n\\n- Server owns the **bounding box** (a clone of the model\'s `PrimaryPart`,\\n  tagged and parented under `BaseUtil.HITBOX_CONTAINER`) and the authoritative\\n  [Replica]. It never builds a visual model.\\n- Client owns the **visual model** (a clone of the prop\'s asset, parented to\\n  `BaseUtil.PROP_CONTAINER`) plus every progress bar, particle, outline and\\n  ProximityPrompt. Its bounding box is handed in by PropController.\\n\\n**Data flow.** All shared state travels through a single Replica of class\\n`BaseUtil.PROP_REPLICA_CLASS`. The server writes with `Set`, the client reacts\\nwith `GetKeyChangedSignal`. Persisted, prop-specific state lives under the\\n`props` key and is reached with [PropBaseClass:GetSavedProps] /\\n[PropBaseClass:SetSavedProp] rather than by touching the replica directly.\\nNothing the client does mutates state on its own \u2014 see below.\\n\\n**Client \u2192 server calls.** The client cannot call methods on the server prop.\\nIt calls [PropBaseClass:DispatchRemoteEvent], which dispatches a\\n`PROP_REMOTE_INPUT` action naming a method; the server routes it through\\n[PropBaseClass:_processRemoteInput], which refuses any method not present in\\nthe prop\'s `_allowedClientFunctions` allowlist. Subclasses extend that\\nallowlist by passing `_allowedClientFunctions` in the `props` table of\\n`new()` (or by calling [PropBaseClass:AllowClientFunction]). Allow-listed\\nmethods receive `player` as their first argument and **must** verify\\nownership themselves with [PropBaseClass:IsOwner] \u2014 the allowlist only gates\\n*which* method may be called, not *by whom*.\\n\\nGated by [FeatureFlags].BaseEnabled \u2014 disabled by default; per-project forks\\nenable it deliberately.\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","tags":["dormant"],"source":{"line":45,"path":"src/Shared/Class/Base/Props/PropBaseClass.luau"}}')}}]);